# Zstandard (zstd) vs gzip for Container Images

A decision reference for adopting zstd compression on container image layers — smaller images, faster pulls, and quicker container startup.

---

## At a glance

| Metric | zstd advantage | Typical numbers |
|---|---|---|
| Compressed size | **10–50% smaller** | 20–30% common; up to ~50% on large / ML images |
| Decompression speed | **50–60%+ faster than pigz** | 2–10× faster than classic gzip |
| Compression speed | **Often faster** (multi-threaded by default) | 5–10× faster than single-thread gzip |
| Startup impact | **Measurable** | AWS Fargate: up to 27% faster task/pod start; ~½ pull time on multi-GB images |

---

## Core findings

- **Algorithm** — Zstandard (zstd) vs gzip.
- **Compressed size** — 10–50% smaller; 20–30% is common, up to ~50% on large or ML-heavy images.
- **Decompression speed** — 50–60%+ faster than pigz; 2–10× faster than classic gzip.
- **Compression speed** — often faster, multi-threaded by default; 5–10× faster than single-thread gzip.
- **Startup impact** — measurable; AWS Fargate shows up to 27% faster task/pod start and roughly half the pull time on multi-GB images.

---

## Why zstd wins for containers

- **Layers** — smaller layers mean less network transfer.
- **Decompression** — dramatically faster, so containers are ready sooner.
- **Compatibility** — supported by BuildKit, containerd, Docker 23+, Podman, CRI-O, and major registries including Vercel.

---

## Vercel relevance

- **Recommendation** — use zstd when pushing to VCR (Vercel Container Registry).
- **Optimization** — feeds into the precompiled snapshot used for Fluid compute and Sandbox quick boots.

---

## Recommended command (Buildx)

Set compression to zstd with level 3 for a good size/speed balance:

```
docker buildx build --push \
  --provenance=false \
  --output type=image,compression=zstd,compression-level=3 \
  -t your-image:tag .
```

- **Level 3** — recommended default: solid size reduction with fast builds.
- **Level 9** — extra size reduction at the cost of longer builds.

